From adfba73fce964122706f12f8ef6674263f68b04c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 18:59:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: mt7996: check if link BSS is initialized before
 dofing vif_link_remove

Problem:
Crash happens on switching an interface to MLD and then to legacy.

Root Cause:
A crash issue could occur with the following command sequence:

change_vif_links: old=0x0, new=0x1
change_vif_links: old=0x1, new=0x0

Since mvif->link[0] always points to vif->drv_priv, if the above command
sequence occurs, mt7996_vif_link_remove() will be called again without
a previous mt7996_vif_link_add().

Solution:
Add a check to ensure mlink->wcid is not NULL before proceeding with
vif link removal operations.

Feature:
Stability

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/commit/c6b206f391358af2fee96389544162838505fd1f
Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
[plcharriere: rebase onto upstream mt7996_vif_link_remove(): return before
the mlink->wcid dereference and set link_id after the check]
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/main.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -464,8 +464,13 @@ void mt7996_vif_link_remove(struct mt76_
 	struct mt7996_vif_link *link = container_of(mlink, struct mt7996_vif_link, mt76);
 	struct mt7996_vif *mvif = (struct mt7996_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
 	struct mt7996_sta_link *msta_link = &link->msta_link;
-	unsigned int link_id = msta_link->wcid.link_id;
 	struct mt7996_phy *phy = mphy->priv;
+	unsigned int link_id;
+
+	if (!mlink->wcid)
+		return;
+
+	link_id = msta_link->wcid.link_id;
 
 	/* Hw requires to destroy active links tearing down the interface, so
 	 * postpone it removing the interface.
